  "query_preview": "/MONDAY THROUGH SATURDAY/...\nIssued at 136 PM MDT Sat Sep 19 2026\n\nMonday and Tuesday...With the northern low out of the region, \ntemporary ridging develops across the Four Corners region as another \nPacific low moves onshore across southern CA and southern NV. Both \nMon and Tue are the coolest days out of the extended period, with \nhigh temps failing to hit 80F. Increasing southwest flow aloft will \nmean a gradual return and moisture to the mts by Tue, but for Mon \ndry conditions will persist for the higher terrain, while the \neastern plains will see some late afternoon and evening convection.\n\nWednesday through Friday...A lot of variability with the extended \nsolutions, though long range models do seem to agree that the \nPacific low ejects to the northeast across the Great Basin on Wed, \nboosting temps slightly due to the increased southwest flow as well \nas increasing precip chances for the mts and southern border. Beyond \nthat, NBM indicates stabilizing temps right around seasonal normals, \nand a daily chance of showers and thunderstorms, more heavily \nweighted towards the mts and the southern border.",
